Sval: a removed tab-scoped DENY reaches the processes holding its site

backport-bug-2064718-tab-permission-removal-every-process.patch sends a
removal to every process that NeedsPermissionsUpdate for the permission's
key, which is the origin's. A DENY is stored for the whole site
(PermissionManager::AddBrowserPermissionInternal), and
TransmitBrowserPermissionsForPrincipal hands it to a process showing any
origin of the site, under that origin. A process that showed only another
origin of the site holds the site's key and not the removed permission's
origin key, so upstream's fix leaves its copy of the DENY in place, and it
applies again on going back there. The removal also goes to the processes
that hold the site's key.

The selection sits inside ForwardBrowserPermissionToChild; no chrome API can
send a permission change to a content process.

diff --git a/extensions/permissions/PermissionManager.cpp b/extensions/permissions/PermissionManager.cpp
index d55e9a7da4..91024de98a 100644
--- a/extensions/permissions/PermissionManager.cpp
+++ b/extensions/permissions/PermissionManager.cpp
@@ -4585,11 +4585,19 @@ void PermissionManager::ForwardBrowserPermissionToChild(
   if (aIsRemoval) {
     nsAutoCString permissionKey;
     GetKeyForPermission(aPrincipal, aType, permissionKey);
+    // Sval: a DENY is stored for the whole site (AddBrowserPermissionInternal),
+    // so TransmitBrowserPermissionsForPrincipal hands it to a process showing
+    // any origin of the site. Such a process holds the site's key and not
+    // this origin's.
+    nsAutoCString siteKey;
+    GetKeyForPrincipal(aPrincipal, IsOAForceStripPermission(aType), true,
+                       siteKey);
 
     nsTArray<dom::ContentParent*> cplist;
     dom::ContentParent::GetAll(cplist);
     for (dom::ContentParent* cp : cplist) {
-      if (cp->NeedsPermissionsUpdate(permissionKey)) {
+      if (cp->NeedsPermissionsUpdate(permissionKey) ||
+          cp->NeedsPermissionsUpdate(siteKey)) {
         (void)cp->SendSetBrowserPermission(origin, nsCString(aType), aAction,
                                            aBrowserId, aIsRemoval);
       }
